    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0201" n="1035" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1035"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9730</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-08T00:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 8, 1918, 12 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 9, 3.20 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4710. War Trade Board, Bureau Enemy Trade [from McFadden]:</p>
                <p>No. 329. Referring your No. 163 of July 2.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d156-f1"/> We
                    have submitted to French Ministry of Blockade and Inter-Allied Black List
                    Committee, Paris, your despatch of July 1<anchor n="2" xml:id="d156-f2"/>
                    regarding creation of the official committee in Paris for the granting of
                    licenses to trade with listed or other enemy persons in Spain, Switzerland and
                    Morocco. French agree in principle to the creation of the committee and to the
                    resolutions as explained in your despatch and are ready to submit all cases
                    which they consider come within the province thereof. The Italian delegate has
                    as yet received no instructions from his Government but is requesting same.
                    British delegate has received authority from his Government to deal with
                    granting licenses to listed persons or firms but no other enemy persons. He has,
                    however, requested wider authority from his Government provided authority [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">other?</hi>] classes of persons, that is a [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">all?</hi>] listed persons or firms and other enemy
                    persons, are covered by your despatch of July 1. We have also communicated with
                    War Trade Board, London, requesting them to ask proper British authorities to
                    confer upon their delegate full authority in this sense. We will keep you
                    informed on these points. McFadden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
